Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 15:48:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03487/11362] [outer-loop] Claude-as-goal-inducer test: FAILS
 on sb26 too -> goal-induction limit is FUNDAMENTAL

Added --dump-prompt + --goal-code (Claude-written goal) + --max-depth to the #3 harness.
Claude (this session) induced sb26's goal from the dumped grid + dynamics: ACTION5 paints
the full-width row-53 bar 2->3, so the most-evidence-supported hypothesis was "fill the
bar". It FAILED (L0, exp=2500, max-depth 80). A decisive diagnostic (spam ACTION5 from
reset) PROVES the hypothesis wrong: ACTION5 paints the bar (bar2s 64->0 by step 40) and
keeps painting all 2s (total 80->20) but LEVEL STAYS 0 -- filling is not the win; ACTION5
is just a paint tool.

CONCLUSION: Claude's best-reasoned goal fails exactly like gemma-4-12B's -> the
goal-induction bottleneck is FUNDAMENTAL (a static first-contact grid + a few action
effects does NOT determine the win condition), NOT the local model. The path forward is
HINDSIGHT goal-induction (ground the goal on an OBSERVED win), blocked by the
chicken-and-egg on games exploration can't crack. So: all four generation-from-scratch
framings (energy-heuristic, energy-fitness-QD, LLM-goal-induction local AND Claude) are
falsified on the hard tail.

verdict: complete: llm_goal_induction_no_winner_honest_null_gap_sharpened (Claude inducer)

